# Force LF in the working tree for the committed study-figure artifact so its
# content hash is byte-stable across platforms. The figure test
# (tests/figures/test_figures.py) hashes the raw JSON bytes; without this, git's
# autocrlf checks the files out as CRLF on Windows and LF on Linux, so the hash
# only matched on the build platform. build_study_artifact._content_hash and the
# test also normalize CRLF -> LF before hashing (the primary, platform-agnostic
# defense); this attribute is belt-and-suspenders so the on-disk bytes match the
# committed (LF) bytes everywhere.
scripts/figures/study_artifact/*.json text eol=lf
